    "next_transformation": "Source-derived closed ordered-dot proof, endpoint-checked affine input streams, shared ordered native product reduction core; scalar/reversed/strided reductions and batched independent output columns. Retain old map DAG on any proof/guard/nonfinite decline. Seed original +0 and preserve every per-output multiply/add/k order, no FMA/reassociation. No benchmark source rewrite, dimensions/names in compiler rules, new runtime ABI/helper/frame/buffer or fee/counter changes.",
    "proof_obligations": [
      "Every original potentially failing body action must belong to the admitted expression closure; dead checked arithmetic or unknown calls prevent the rewrite.",
      "Every checked affine selector subexpression and logical axis has valid first/last endpoints; monotonic affine interior is therefore safe. Linear column-major selection needs vector geometry or a same-logical-column proof, otherwise use original checked DAG.",
      "Batch parent must resolve to exactly one admitted child dot or invariant F64 alternative through its exact U64 comparison/Boolean source CFG. Retain source visits/fees and fill every original output position.",
      "Only private final results may be written before complete success. Any invalid endpoint, shape, unexpected current view or nonfinite fast result resumes the untouched original checked DAG before publication.",
      "Share the same strict F64Mul/F64Add ordered kernel with products; SIMD lanes are independent outputs, never partial sums of one reduction. Existing scalar/product direct paths, private loans, replay and accounting remain."
    ],
